      "type": "title",
      "headline": "How a recommender's embedding lookups train on the GPU",
      "sub": "Meta's Triton rewrite of the table-batched embedding, forward and backward.",
      "punch": [
        "Gather is easy.",
        "Scatter is not."
      ],
      "say": "Hi, I'm Abacus! Recommenders learn from ids, and the kernel that looks them up just moved from CUDA to Triton. Here's how it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "idea",
      "text": "The backward win is mostly a threshold: Triton keeps runs of up to 256 lookups on one simple program, where CUDA starts cooperating at 32.",
      "mark": "mostly a threshold",
      "say": "The idea: most of the backward win comes from where each kernel changes strategy, not from a new algorithm."
    },
